INFO  [Claude Code] **Problem**: `NumberFormatException` when parsing BigDecimal values (missing "e" notation exponential mark)
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Solution**: Created a factory method `createSettlementsWithValidBigDecimals()` that produces a `Settlements` object containing three properly initialized `Settlement` objects with valid `BigDecimal` values. All BigDecimal fields are initialized using proper string constructors (e.g., `new BigDecimal("1000.00")`) to avoid parsing errors.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### 2. Issue 2 & 3 - BrownianMotionOracleTestFactory
INFO  [Claude Code] **File**: `src/test/java/net/finmath/smartcontract/valuation/oracle/simulated/BrownianMotionOracleTestFactory.java`
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Problem**: 
INFO  [Claude Code] - Issue 2: `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` with index -1 when using no-arg constructor
INFO  [Claude Code] - Issue 3: `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` with index 10 when using parameterized constructor
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Solution**: Created three factory methods:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. **`createBrownianMotionOracleWithFixedTime()`** - Uses a fixed initial time (2000-01-01) instead of `LocalDateTime.now()` to avoid negative index issues when getValue is called with historical times.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. **`createBrownianMotionOracleWithValidTimeDiscretization()`** - Creates an oracle with a 10-year time horizon and daily steps, providing approximately 3650 time points to handle most test scenarios.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] 3. **`createBrownianMotionOracleWithExtendedHorizon()`** - Creates an oracle with a 30-year time horizon to provide even more flexibility for various test cases.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] All factory methods are properly annotated with `@com.diffblue.cover.annotations.InterestingTestFactory` as required.
